# Ling 3.2 Flash — findings by Iceman

- Source: Ant Group / inclusionAI / Ling 3.2 Flash
- Date: 2026-11-14 (UTC), deep second-pass research
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Ling-3.2-flash
- **Short description:** Ant Group/inclusionAI Ling-series native multimodal MoE model positioned for complex visual understanding, multimodal long-horizon agents, 3D understanding/interaction, and medical multimodal tasks.
- **Provider / access:** Ant Ling developer platform / Ant Bailian and third-party platforms per official docs. OpenRouter lists `inclusionai/ling-3.2-flash` (page accessible in this pass), but HF model page access returned 401 and AA/model-catalog benchmark pages were not found. Local metadata lists `opencode/ling-3.2-flash`, `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Ant Ling official model documentation reviewed 2026-11-14. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed sources.
- **IDs:** `Ling-3.2-flash`, `ling-3.2-flash`, `inclusionai/ling-3.2-flash`, `opencode/ling-3.2-flash`.
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 tokens (Ant Ling docs/local metadata).
- **Modalities:** Text, image, and video input; text output (Ant Ling docs).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** $0.30 / $0.90 per 1M input/output tokens on Ant Bailian launch pricing per local metadata (time-limited trial noted); pricing/availability may vary by platform. No standing free ID indicated in local metadata.
- **Architecture:** Native multimodal MoE, **560B total / 25B activated parameters** (Ant Ling docs/local metadata).

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): I performed a deep second-pass review of Ant Ling official model documentation, OpenRouter model/catalog pages, models.dev/AA search/fetch attempts, Hugging Face/model listing attempts (including 401 on HF model page), ModelScope/GitHub fetches, and local metadata/prior report. Official docs provide attributable identity/spec/capability details for this exact model, but **no independently verifiable standardized public benchmark numerics** for this project’s comparison dimensions (Terminal-Bench/Tau/GDPval-AA/Toolathon/MCP-Atlas, GPQA/HLE/AIME/AA Intelligence Index/LCR, SWE-bench/LiveCodeBench/SciCode, MMMU/MMMU-Pro/WebVoyager/MMSearch, etc.) were found in accessible sources. OpenRouter page text scanned in this pass did not expose attributable AA benchmark values for this model. Because evidence is insufficient for comparable normalized scoring, this file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

Agent / tool use:

- Official docs position Ling-3.2-flash for multimodal long-horizon agents and complex real-world tasks, but no standardized agent/tool benchmark numerics found.
- Terminal-Bench 2.1 / Tau2 / Tau3 / GDPval-AA / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: **no verified public score found**

Reasoning / knowledge:

- Official docs describe deep reasoning and multimodal understanding capabilities; no standardized reasoning/knowledge benchmark numerics found.
- GPQA Diamond / HLE / AIME / AA Intelligence Index: **no verified public score found**

Coding:

- Coding-agent benchmark evidence not publicly verified in accessible official/catalog sources; no standardized coding numerics found.
- SWE-bench Verified / SWE-Pro / LiveCodeBench / SciCode: **no verified public score found**

Long context:

- 1M context window stated in official docs/local metadata; no standalone long-context retrieval benchmark score found.

Multimodal:

- Native image/text/video input and multimodal capability areas (complex visual understanding, 3D understanding/interaction, medical multimodal) described in official docs; no standardized multimodal benchmark numerics found.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not provided. Insufficient independently verifiable standardized public benchmark evidence for this exact model in reviewed official and public catalog sources; assigning normalized 1–100 scores would be speculative/non-comparable. No scored assessment is issued and this report remains self-excluded.

### Source comparison / conflicts

- **Specs/capabilities:** Ant Ling docs and local metadata align on core identity (Ling-3.2-flash, 560B/25B MoE, 1M context, native image/text/video input, multimodal/agent focus).
- **Access/pricing:** Local metadata cites Ant Bailian launch pricing ($0.30/$0.90 per 1M) and no standing free ID; OpenRouter lists an `inclusionai/ling-3.2-flash` page but benchmark/spec details were limited in accessible text.
- **Benchmarks:** No verified standardized benchmark numerics found across Ant Ling docs, OpenRouter page scan, AA/models.dev/HF attempts. HF model page access was unauthorized (401) in this pass.

